# Oracle: VD cmd-analysis-ac (stepped, lin by intervals: points+1 values, dec and oct per
# decade/octave, values list); IR sweep.rs (`points` is the number of values: VACASK's reader
# adds one to a lin count, as an integer literal or `+ 1`, and takes `x - 1`, the writer's
# spelling of the count `x`, back as `x`: law L5 seed found it).
# codes:
file "ac.sim" deck
  title "ac sweeps"
  analysis ac name=a1 (lin start=1k stop=2k step=100i)
  analysis ac name=a2 (lin start=1k stop=2k points=11i)
  analysis ac name=a3 (dec start=1i stop=1g points=10i)
  analysis ac name=a4 (oct start=1i stop=1k points=3i)
  analysis ac name=a5 (list values=[1k, 2k, 5k])
  analysis ac name=a6 (dec start=1i stop=1k points=n?)
  analysis ac name=a7 (lin start=1i stop=1k points=n?)
  analysis ac name=a8 (lin start=1i stop=1k points=(n? + 1i))
